{"id": "EUVD-2026-106898", "enisaUuid": "8ff98aae-6c93-3ee8-ba54-21abc6f6a36c", "description": "Dulwich before 1.2.9 contains a denial of service vulnerability in Pack.resolve_object that allows attackers to cause infinite recursion via self-referential OFS_DELTA objects. Attackers can supply a malicious packfile with an OFS_DELTA delta_offset of 0 to exhaust CPU during clone, fetch, or cat-file operations.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T00:36:59", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T15:49:44", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/jelmer/dulwich/security/advisories/GHSA-35mr-4567-66vg", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/dulwich-before-1.2.9-infinite-loop-dos-via-pack-resolve-object"], "aliases": ["GHSA-r78r-wr5r-rqfm", "CVE-2026-114095"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.25, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "cc02644e-cd73-3ea7-addf-78d4ca729b6f", "product": {"name": "dulwich", "vendor": {"name": "jelmer"}}, "product_version": "0 <1.2.9"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "13b5ab52-cbe3-3e82-af0b-d2e1c4ee19e4", "vendor": {"name": "jelmer"}}], "isExploited": false}